  "order": 22,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "9yklybw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Definition of Matter"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Matter is composed of minute particles that possess mass, occupy volume, and exhibit continuous kinetic movement.",
        "The five physical states of matter are Solid, Liquid, Gas, Plasma, and Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC).",
        "Sublimation is the direct phase transition from solid to gas without entering the liquid state.",
        "Latent heat is energy absorbed or released during a state transition occurring at a constant temperature.",
        "Evaporation is a surface phenomenon that causes cooling and increases with higher surface area, temperature, and wind speed."
      ],
      "id": "1rgneie"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "States of Matter",
          "value": "5 States",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
