      ],
      "id": "2ph3fbc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7v2r30l",
      "content": "Matter is anything that has mass and occupies space."
    },
    {
      "id": "u0gv0sg",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "rtdqtrh",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_rtdqtrh.png"
    },
    {
      "id": "i4brcse",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "uy96mt0",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB GS/images/image_uy96mt0.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aoow5ru",
      "content": "Matter is made up of extremely small particles called atoms and molecules."
    },
    {
      "id": "c8iuse7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Characteristics of Particles of Matter"
    },
    {
      "id": "2dxjf2a",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        " Particles have space between them.",
        " Particles are continuously moving (kinetic energy).",
        "Particles attract each other.",
        "Force of attraction: Solid &gt; Liquid &gt; Gas.",
        "Kinetic energy: Gas &gt; Liquid &gt; Solid."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1p78pvk",
