      "level": 2,
      "content": "Solution, Suspension and Colloid"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xnlfe8n",
      "content": "Solution: Homogeneous mixture (particle size &lt; 1 nm)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aatrcve",
      "content": "Suspension: Visible particles, unstable."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qg4vs8k",
      "content": "Colloid: Intermediate size, shows Tyndall effect."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "83b9s3j",
      "content": "Particle size order: Solution &lt; Colloid &lt; Suspension."
    },
    {
      "id": "dtfba5d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Separation Techniques"
    },
    {
      "id": "ng236ja",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Evaporation – Salt from water",
        " Centrifugation – Cream from milk",
        "Distillation – Separating liquids",
        "Chromatography – Ink colours",
        "Crystallization – Purification of solids"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Steam at 100°C causes more severe burns than boiling water at 100°C due to the high latent heat of vaporization.",
        "Solid Carbon Dioxide (Dry Ice) sublimates directly into gas at 1 atmosphere pressure without melting.",
        "Colloids and suspensions display the Tyndall effect (scattering of light), whereas true solutions do not.",
        "Bose-Einstein Condensate (BEC) is formed by cooling a gas of extremely low density to super-low temperatures."
      ],
      "id": "4lpf670"
    },
